1
00:00:14,077 --> 00:00:17,038
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:20,166 --> 00:00:22,210
Did the association get
this year's donation?

3
00:00:22,710 --> 00:00:24,045
They did, sir.

4
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:28,883
2026 NATIONAL SPORTS FESTIVAL
HIGH SCHOOL TEAM LINEUP

5
00:00:31,219 --> 00:00:34,264
COACH: HONG DO-YEOP
ASSISTANT COACH: JANG TAE-HA

6
00:00:37,350 --> 00:00:38,476
Hong Do-yeop.

7
00:00:39,352 --> 00:00:40,603
Jang Tae-ha.

8
00:00:42,272 --> 00:00:43,606
They're together?

9
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:51,948
So the man who despised anyone
who fought outside the ring

10
00:00:53,241 --> 00:00:55,660
took back his precious disciple.

11
00:00:56,578 --> 00:00:58,705
The pride of Gujin, Kim Pil-seung!

12
00:00:58,788 --> 00:01:00,623
You've got this!

13
00:01:12,927 --> 00:01:14,137
He's got this.

14
00:01:15,346 --> 00:01:17,765
That's not what she should be doing
right about now.

15
00:01:24,105 --> 00:01:27,233
Before I lost my memory,

16
00:01:27,317 --> 00:01:28,276
maybe I was a pro…

17
00:01:29,736 --> 00:01:31,070
A prodigy!

18
00:01:31,571 --> 00:01:33,865
-You were amazing.
-You're smart.

19
00:01:35,116 --> 00:01:36,701
She lost her memory?

20
00:01:39,996 --> 00:01:41,372
We found her location.

21
00:01:42,290 --> 00:01:45,084
It's said that she lives in Gujin
with Jang Tae-ha.

22
00:01:47,128 --> 00:01:48,880
I need to see for myself.

23
00:02:11,194 --> 00:02:12,612
Is this yours, sir?

24
00:02:37,262 --> 00:02:38,096
Thank you.

25
00:02:39,847 --> 00:02:40,848
No problem.

26
00:02:47,188 --> 00:02:48,481
But

27
00:02:49,274 --> 00:02:51,234
is that really yours?

28
00:02:53,194 --> 00:02:54,988
It looks like a woman's watch.

29
00:03:04,455 --> 00:03:05,290
Does it?

30
00:03:05,373 --> 00:03:07,250
You have a keen eye.

31
00:03:07,834 --> 00:03:10,253
It's clearly too small for your wrist.

32
00:03:13,298 --> 00:03:14,424
It used to be a woman's…

33
00:03:16,426 --> 00:03:18,011
but now it's mine.

34
00:03:22,765 --> 00:03:23,599
Okay.

35
00:03:29,147 --> 00:03:30,273
I'll see you again.

36
00:03:38,990 --> 00:03:40,158
What's wrong with me?

37
00:03:41,534 --> 00:03:43,453
It's not even cold, but I have the chills.

38
00:03:57,800 --> 00:04:01,596
The thing is, I've never seen him
around the village before.

39
00:04:01,679 --> 00:04:04,140
He was wearing
a really nice and expensive suit

40
00:04:04,223 --> 00:04:07,643
and had a full head of hair
and these super intense eyes.

41
00:04:08,353 --> 00:04:11,689
But what's weird is
he had a woman's watch.

42
00:04:12,190 --> 00:04:14,150
-Do you know who he is?
-I sure do.

43
00:04:15,068 --> 00:04:15,902
Who is he?

44
00:04:15,985 --> 00:04:17,862
What do you think it means

45
00:04:17,945 --> 00:04:21,240
when a man with intense eyes goes around
wearing a woman's watch?

46
00:04:21,949 --> 00:04:24,494
It means he's lost his marbles.

47
00:04:31,084 --> 00:04:32,752
You're here, Song-wol.

48
00:04:36,798 --> 00:04:37,632
PAYCHECK

49
00:04:37,715 --> 00:04:39,967
What's this? "Paycheck"?

50
00:04:41,886 --> 00:04:45,765
Wait, I get paid?

51
00:04:46,516 --> 00:04:47,934
Yay me!

52
00:04:50,645 --> 00:04:52,772
It's cute, my paycheck.

53
00:04:53,398 --> 00:04:57,819
Now that you got paid,
why not buy yourself some new clothes?

54
00:04:58,319 --> 00:05:01,989
You like to dress up, don't you?

55
00:05:13,376 --> 00:05:14,460
So,

56
00:05:14,544 --> 00:05:19,674
you're saying that you're Baek Sang-gil,
Chairman of Mirae Eden.

57
00:05:19,757 --> 00:05:23,344
But why did you come to see me?

58
00:05:23,428 --> 00:05:25,388
If you don't mind me asking.

59
00:05:26,055 --> 00:05:29,183
Why did you meet Gwak Chi-hyeon, Doctor?

60
00:05:31,227 --> 00:05:32,895
Prosecutor Go… I mean, Go Ji-won

61
00:05:32,979 --> 00:05:36,023
was an amnesia patient
who came to see me about a month ago.

62
00:05:36,774 --> 00:05:39,527
She was suspicious
of her current boyfriend,

63
00:05:39,610 --> 00:05:42,822
and one day, she said she remembered
a man named Gwak Chi-hyeon.

64
00:05:42,905 --> 00:05:45,616
She wanted to know the truth,

65
00:05:45,700 --> 00:05:49,662
so I tracked him down and met with him.

66
00:05:51,164 --> 00:05:54,917
Then why did you tell Gwak Chi-hyeon
that you didn't know Prosecutor Go?

67
00:06:00,590 --> 00:06:03,217
I was scared.

68
00:06:04,260 --> 00:06:07,221
It seems as though
something big is going on,

69
00:06:07,305 --> 00:06:09,390
and I'd rather not get involved.

70
00:06:09,474 --> 00:06:12,977
I'm just a regular doctor
who runs a small clinic in the country.

71
00:06:13,978 --> 00:06:16,522
I really don't know anything.

72
00:06:17,023 --> 00:06:22,487
So I would be very grateful
if you could please leave now.

73
00:06:28,951 --> 00:06:31,621
When do you think
Prosecutor Go will get her memory back?

74
00:06:33,456 --> 00:06:34,749
That's impossible to know.

75
00:06:34,832 --> 00:06:35,958
Aren't you her doctor?

76
00:06:36,542 --> 00:06:38,336
I'm her doctor, yes. Not a fortune…

77
00:06:40,588 --> 00:06:42,715
I'm sorry. That came out a bit…

78
00:06:54,519 --> 00:06:56,687
There must be a way
to get her memory back quicker,

79
00:06:58,356 --> 00:06:59,440
mustn't there?

80
00:07:18,751 --> 00:07:19,919
Tae-ha.

81
00:08:20,313 --> 00:08:21,397
Hands off.

82
00:08:40,750 --> 00:08:42,543
You can kill me, sir.

83
00:08:43,044 --> 00:08:44,629
You don't have to kill me nicely.

84
00:08:44,712 --> 00:08:49,091
You can do whatever you want to me
until your anger is gone.

85
00:08:52,386 --> 00:08:53,220
Please…

86
00:08:57,725 --> 00:09:00,061
Please just spare Prosecutor Go's life.

87
00:09:03,356 --> 00:09:05,107
She doesn't have her memory right now.

88
00:09:05,191 --> 00:09:07,485
She doesn't even know
that she was a prosecutor.

89
00:09:07,985 --> 00:09:10,321
She can't do you any harm, sir.

90
00:09:14,575 --> 00:09:15,660
Tae-ha.

91
00:09:18,913 --> 00:09:19,747
Yes?

92
00:09:22,333 --> 00:09:23,542
Enough with the melodrama.

93
00:09:29,924 --> 00:09:31,425
Why did you let her live?

94
00:09:39,558 --> 00:09:41,602
She's someone I owed from a long time ago.

95
00:09:55,032 --> 00:09:58,703
The Jang Tae-ha, who worked like a machine
for 14 years without a single slipup,

96
00:10:00,037 --> 00:10:03,249
did all this because of
some petty sentiment?

97
00:10:30,025 --> 00:10:30,943
Come with me.

98
00:10:57,511 --> 00:10:59,555
Say hi to your boys. It's been a while.

99
00:11:10,232 --> 00:11:12,401
Had they served you well,

100
00:11:13,402 --> 00:11:15,529
you never would have made
the wrong choice.

101
00:11:16,655 --> 00:11:18,157
Such a shame.

102
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,116
No!

103
00:11:23,496 --> 00:11:24,705
Sir!

104
00:11:27,666 --> 00:11:29,001
Jang Tae-ha, don't move!

105
00:11:34,924 --> 00:11:36,884
The boys are to blame for that.

106
00:11:39,345 --> 00:11:40,429
Please stop!

107
00:11:41,722 --> 00:11:42,556
Sir!

108
00:11:43,057 --> 00:11:44,850
Hurt me instead!

109
00:11:44,934 --> 00:11:47,311
Come on, that's not right.

110
00:11:47,937 --> 00:11:50,022
You know how fond I was of you.

111
00:11:50,105 --> 00:11:52,483
I'd never do something
this childish to you.

112
00:11:53,651 --> 00:11:54,735
Sir!

113
00:11:56,654 --> 00:11:58,405
No, don't!

114
00:11:59,323 --> 00:12:00,407
Tae-ha, sir!

115
00:12:00,491 --> 00:12:01,408
Sir!

116
00:12:04,787 --> 00:12:05,788
Tae-ha!

117
00:12:45,911 --> 00:12:48,247
Throughout both Eastern
and Western history,

118
00:12:49,164 --> 00:12:52,960
people didn't use guns or knives
to torture the worst of them.

119
00:12:58,424 --> 00:13:01,510
Instead, they covered their eyes
with a single black cloth.

120
00:13:03,095 --> 00:13:06,640
The fear of not knowing what will happen
is scarier than any gun or knife.

121
00:13:09,059 --> 00:13:10,561
I know what you're planning.

122
00:13:10,644 --> 00:13:12,563
Go on and try.

123
00:13:12,646 --> 00:13:17,568
But every day, your imagination will
eat away at you, wondering about my plan…

124
00:13:19,361 --> 00:13:20,654
for you…

125
00:13:23,032 --> 00:13:24,950
and Prosecutor Go.

126
00:13:30,789 --> 00:13:33,459
Escort Director Jang home,

127
00:13:34,835 --> 00:13:35,794
respectfully.

128
00:13:47,056 --> 00:13:50,392
Jang Tae-ha seems unaware of the extra
evidence Gwak Chi-hyeon mentioned.

129
00:13:50,476 --> 00:13:54,563
If he had it, he wouldn't have begged.
He would have tried to negotiate.

130
00:13:58,776 --> 00:14:02,446
Only Prosecutor Go knows
where that evidence is.

131
00:14:04,865 --> 00:14:06,283
But she can't remember.

132
00:14:07,534 --> 00:14:09,036
If we just take care of her now--

133
00:14:09,119 --> 00:14:13,415
No. That bitch, Prosecutor Go,
must have had a plan B.

134
00:14:17,378 --> 00:14:20,881
If it's buried somewhere
and manages to surface somehow,

135
00:14:20,965 --> 00:14:22,925
it'll be the end for me and Mayor Ju.

136
00:14:23,008 --> 00:14:24,426
We must find and destroy it.

137
00:14:27,596 --> 00:14:28,847
In order to do that…

138
00:14:34,561 --> 00:14:36,772
we have to stir Prosecutor Go's memory.

139
00:14:39,692 --> 00:14:40,901
Hey, Tae-ha.

140
00:14:41,735 --> 00:14:44,655
Tae-ha, what did you mean by that?

141
00:14:44,738 --> 00:14:45,948
Baek Sang-gil was here?

142
00:14:46,031 --> 00:14:47,324
Did you meet him?

143
00:14:49,243 --> 00:14:51,036
Is Eun-sae okay?

144
00:14:52,454 --> 00:14:54,039
I have to go somewhere now.

145
00:14:54,623 --> 00:14:57,084
I'll tell you the details when I get back.

146
00:14:57,584 --> 00:14:59,378
Please protect Eun-sae while I'm gone.

147
00:14:59,461 --> 00:15:00,754
-Okay.
-Of course.

148
00:15:08,053 --> 00:15:09,680
Goodness.

149
00:15:14,768 --> 00:15:15,728
Jang Tae-ha.

150
00:15:16,228 --> 00:15:19,106
Gi-jun, I need your help.

151
00:15:21,734 --> 00:15:24,028
No, I don't want to. I won't.

152
00:15:24,111 --> 00:15:28,741
I really don't want to be involved
in this anymore.

153
00:15:28,824 --> 00:15:29,992
Go Eun-sae has amnesia.

154
00:15:30,659 --> 00:15:33,746
Now's the best time to deal with her
before her memory returns.

155
00:15:34,371 --> 00:15:37,458
And yet, Baek Sang-gil kept her alive.
Why do you think that is?

156
00:15:38,542 --> 00:15:39,835
How would I know?

157
00:15:39,918 --> 00:15:41,754
I'm asking because I have a hunch.

158
00:15:42,504 --> 00:15:43,839
You meeting Gwak Chi-hyeon.

159
00:15:43,922 --> 00:15:45,174
What about that?

160
00:15:45,257 --> 00:15:47,509
I made sure Gwak Chi-hyeon
couldn't make a move.

161
00:15:47,593 --> 00:15:50,012
But he was wandering around,
searching for Go Eun-sae.

162
00:15:50,721 --> 00:15:53,599
That means Baek Sang-gil
still has a use for him.

163
00:15:53,682 --> 00:15:56,018
He must need something more
from Go Eun-sae.

164
00:15:56,101 --> 00:15:57,686
We need to find out what that is.

165
00:15:59,188 --> 00:16:00,481
Gi-jun, please.

166
00:16:01,148 --> 00:16:02,357
You're my only hope.

167
00:16:04,359 --> 00:16:07,738
I really don't want to. You…

168
00:16:08,363 --> 00:16:12,534
We're not close, so you must not know,
but I'm a huge scaredy-cat.

169
00:16:13,202 --> 00:16:15,579
I can't watch Unanswered Questions.
It freaks me out.

170
00:16:15,662 --> 00:16:18,916
What's that show called?
Surprise Mystery TV: Truth or Fiction?

171
00:16:18,999 --> 00:16:21,960
I can't watch it
because it makes my heart race.

172
00:16:22,836 --> 00:16:24,963
Gi-jun, please help me.

173
00:16:26,256 --> 00:16:27,132
I said I won't--

174
00:16:28,092 --> 00:16:29,426
What…

175
00:16:30,803 --> 00:16:31,887
Su-ji.

176
00:16:31,970 --> 00:16:33,722
I left something behind.

177
00:16:33,806 --> 00:16:35,516
This day's driving me crazy.

178
00:16:36,517 --> 00:16:39,520
What does Jang Tae-ha want you
to help him with?

179
00:16:40,354 --> 00:16:41,188
What?

180
00:16:48,278 --> 00:16:50,197
Okay, fine.

181
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:55,327
Let's hear what it is
you want me to help you with.

182
00:16:56,078 --> 00:16:56,995
What is it?

183
00:17:01,333 --> 00:17:06,046
CHEONAN SAMGEORI REST STOP

184
00:17:26,608 --> 00:17:28,819
What did he say? Did you find out?

185
00:17:30,988 --> 00:17:33,782
When do you think
Prosecutor Go will get her memory back?

186
00:17:33,866 --> 00:17:37,244
Why would Chairman Baek Sang-gil…

187
00:17:38,203 --> 00:17:39,621
Why would he come to you…

188
00:17:44,001 --> 00:17:45,752
To be honest,

189
00:17:45,836 --> 00:17:49,298
I prefer to stay out of messy affairs,
so I played dumb.

190
00:17:49,381 --> 00:17:51,925
But since the chairman himself

191
00:17:52,009 --> 00:17:54,386
came all the way
to ask me about Go Ji-won,

192
00:17:55,137 --> 00:17:57,306
I think it's time I knew
what's going down.

193
00:17:58,515 --> 00:18:02,936
What does Chairman Baek want
from Prosecutor Go?

194
00:18:04,771 --> 00:18:07,065
Why would I tell you that?

195
00:18:07,149 --> 00:18:09,026
How could I trust you?

196
00:18:12,613 --> 00:18:14,948
I made sure Gwak Chi-hyeon
couldn't make a move.

197
00:18:16,408 --> 00:18:18,076
I heard you almost died.

198
00:18:19,119 --> 00:18:20,495
Please, no!

199
00:18:22,247 --> 00:18:23,081
No!

200
00:18:27,461 --> 00:18:31,340
Wait. How do you even know about that?

201
00:18:31,924 --> 00:18:33,175
Chairman Baek told me.

202
00:18:39,723 --> 00:18:41,516
I'm sure you know very well

203
00:18:41,600 --> 00:18:43,143
that for people like us,

204
00:18:43,227 --> 00:18:46,396
the moment we are rendered useless,
we're done.

205
00:18:46,897 --> 00:18:50,192
But now that the chairman
has actually found Go Ji-won,

206
00:18:50,275 --> 00:18:53,028
we need to be of help to him in some way

207
00:18:53,111 --> 00:18:55,113
in order for us both to live.

208
00:18:55,989 --> 00:18:56,907
Don't you think?

209
00:19:00,577 --> 00:19:02,537
Let's find it together.

210
00:19:03,538 --> 00:19:04,748
How we can be of help.

211
00:19:06,583 --> 00:19:07,834
What is it

212
00:19:08,418 --> 00:19:12,005
that the chairman wants
from Prosecutor Go?

213
00:19:13,340 --> 00:19:15,467
Chairman Baek Sang-gil
and Mayor Ju Min-jong.

214
00:19:15,550 --> 00:19:18,136
There's another piece of evidence
linking them.

215
00:19:21,431 --> 00:19:23,141
Never make me do this again.

216
00:19:24,726 --> 00:19:27,938
It was no easy feat, you know.

217
00:19:28,522 --> 00:19:31,483
He's not exactly the talkative type.

218
00:19:31,566 --> 00:19:35,529
But since I'm a psychiatrist
and I understand human psychology,

219
00:19:35,612 --> 00:19:37,864
I have a way with words.

220
00:19:37,948 --> 00:19:42,703
You should know
that I got him to talk on pure skill.

221
00:19:43,203 --> 00:19:44,538
Yeah, thanks.

222
00:19:44,621 --> 00:19:46,331
Hey, I'm not done.

223
00:19:49,626 --> 00:19:52,004
Would it be okay
if I heard you out another time?

224
00:19:52,087 --> 00:19:53,380
No, it's not that.

225
00:19:55,340 --> 00:19:56,174
This.

226
00:20:00,137 --> 00:20:02,556
I bought this on my way to Seoul.

227
00:20:03,056 --> 00:20:08,353
It's the latest model
that detects all wiretaps and GPS devices.

228
00:20:08,854 --> 00:20:12,524
What if Baek Sang-gil planted something
while watching you?

229
00:20:13,275 --> 00:20:16,903
I also bought one and checked,
but there was nothing, at least in my car.

230
00:20:16,987 --> 00:20:20,657
And still, I'm whispering like this.
You always have to be vigilant.

231
00:20:26,371 --> 00:20:29,666
Thanks, Gi-jun.
I'll make sure to repay you for your help.

232
00:20:30,292 --> 00:20:31,209
Don't mention it.

233
00:20:39,926 --> 00:20:41,636
Guess I'm pretty damn cool too.

234
00:20:48,060 --> 00:20:50,604
What? Information
about the stowaway boat plan leaked?

235
00:20:50,687 --> 00:20:54,274
It seems so. I lost contact
with one of the Japanese brokers.

236
00:20:55,108 --> 00:20:56,526
I know what you're planning.

237
00:20:57,110 --> 00:20:58,695
Go on and try.

238
00:21:02,616 --> 00:21:04,201
Can we arrange another date?

239
00:21:04,284 --> 00:21:06,161
Not unless we want a serious delay.

240
00:21:06,745 --> 00:21:09,706
Can you at least change the time
the boat leaves that day?

241
00:21:10,332 --> 00:21:11,541
I'm relying on you, Kaito.

242
00:21:11,625 --> 00:21:14,336
Just like in Namba, Osaka, ten years ago.

243
00:21:20,092 --> 00:21:22,386
There's nothing in our gym.

244
00:21:25,597 --> 00:21:28,183
Baek Sang-gil never leaves loose ends.

245
00:21:28,266 --> 00:21:30,102
Now that he knows there's more evidence,

246
00:21:30,185 --> 00:21:33,271
he won't kill Go Eun-sae
until he finds and destroys it.

247
00:21:34,689 --> 00:21:37,526
In a way, it's lucky she lost her memory.

248
00:21:39,194 --> 00:21:41,655
The best move is to smuggle her out
as soon as possible.

249
00:21:42,447 --> 00:21:45,742
We need to send Go Eun-sae away
this Thursday, no matter what.

250
00:21:46,743 --> 00:21:47,744
And you?

251
00:21:48,662 --> 00:21:49,955
Will you be okay?

252
00:21:52,165 --> 00:21:52,999
Yes.

253
00:21:53,500 --> 00:21:56,545
Baek Sang-gil will think
there's a chance I have the evidence,

254
00:21:56,628 --> 00:21:58,713
so he won't do anything rash.

255
00:22:02,926 --> 00:22:03,760
I'll be going now.

256
00:22:05,011 --> 00:22:05,929
Okay.

257
00:22:06,638 --> 00:22:07,514
Go on.

258
00:22:15,188 --> 00:22:16,523
What do we do?

259
00:22:17,023 --> 00:22:18,650
Will Tae-ha really be okay?

260
00:22:18,733 --> 00:22:20,193
He's not a fool.

261
00:22:20,277 --> 00:22:23,697
I'm sure he's already got a plan
in that head of his.

262
00:22:26,825 --> 00:22:28,743
How will he ever send Eun-sae away?

263
00:22:28,827 --> 00:22:32,539
And how will Eun-sae go on without Tae-ha?

264
00:22:32,622 --> 00:22:36,293
Yeah, it's not like people can control
how they feel.

265
00:22:36,877 --> 00:22:39,212
How do you break a bond
that's grown so deep?

266
00:22:45,719 --> 00:22:46,553
Here!

267
00:22:46,636 --> 00:22:47,804
My paycheck got this.

268
00:22:49,931 --> 00:22:52,392
It was my first paycheck
after losing my memory.

269
00:22:52,476 --> 00:22:55,228
And I was thinking, "What should I buy?"

270
00:22:55,729 --> 00:23:00,484
People say, if nothing else,
that good shoes are a must.

271
00:23:01,943 --> 00:23:03,445
You should have treated yourself.

272
00:23:04,779 --> 00:23:07,532
I already have everything I want.

273
00:23:11,620 --> 00:23:14,581
No matter how much I think about it,
all I need is Jang Tae-ha.

274
00:23:19,544 --> 00:23:21,213
What's with that face?

275
00:23:23,465 --> 00:23:25,467
Is it because of that superstition

276
00:23:25,550 --> 00:23:28,094
that if you give someone shoes,
they'll run away?

277
00:23:29,387 --> 00:23:31,890
I gave them to you
with a different meaning.

278
00:23:37,979 --> 00:23:40,524
From now on, let's walk together.

279
00:23:45,278 --> 00:23:48,782
So, from now on,
no need to try so hard on your own.

280
00:23:49,282 --> 00:23:50,867
Let's do everything together.

281
00:23:54,955 --> 00:23:56,331
Speaking of which…

282
00:24:09,386 --> 00:24:11,221
Put it towards your grandma's meds.

283
00:24:14,474 --> 00:24:15,475
Go Eun-sae.

284
00:24:22,816 --> 00:24:24,025
You're touched.

285
00:24:26,820 --> 00:24:30,407
Well, I guess
I just like Jang Tae-ha that much.

286
00:24:59,811 --> 00:25:02,314
From now on, let's walk together.

287
00:25:26,379 --> 00:25:28,173
I looked into what you asked me to.

288
00:25:28,798 --> 00:25:29,633
It's possible.

289
00:25:30,258 --> 00:25:31,092
Good work.

290
00:25:31,593 --> 00:25:34,220
And I just transferred some money
to your account.

291
00:25:34,304 --> 00:25:36,389
Send it to the guys who got hurt today.

292
00:25:37,140 --> 00:25:39,809
-Sir, you don't have to--
-They got hurt because of me.

293
00:25:42,145 --> 00:25:44,689
How did you survive that world
with such a soft heart?

294
00:25:46,191 --> 00:25:48,902
And how will you ever send her away?

295
00:25:53,239 --> 00:25:55,492
She didn't even buy
the clothes she wanted today

296
00:25:55,575 --> 00:25:57,160
so she could buy you a present.

297
00:25:59,371 --> 00:26:01,206
You like each other so much.

298
00:26:01,956 --> 00:26:05,418
How will you two live
after you send her away?

299
00:26:10,965 --> 00:26:11,800
Speaking of which…

300
00:26:16,596 --> 00:26:18,306
I'm going to need everyone's help.

301
00:26:30,568 --> 00:26:31,945
Are you going somewhere today?

302
00:26:36,741 --> 00:26:37,992
To work.

303
00:26:48,461 --> 00:26:49,713
What work?

304
00:26:50,213 --> 00:26:52,298
Surely, you're not going
to the gym like that?

305
00:26:55,301 --> 00:26:57,470
Jang Tae-ha, wait.

306
00:26:58,680 --> 00:27:00,432
This isn't right.

307
00:27:00,515 --> 00:27:02,934
You're really going to go back
to that life?

308
00:27:03,017 --> 00:27:05,645
I found a hospital
specializing in geriatric cancer care.

309
00:27:05,729 --> 00:27:06,730
For Grandma's surgery.

310
00:27:07,939 --> 00:27:10,942
I can't afford the hospital bills
with my salary from the gym.

311
00:27:12,110 --> 00:27:13,403
Still, this is wrong.

312
00:27:14,320 --> 00:27:16,448
How can you go back to being a gangster?

313
00:27:17,991 --> 00:27:19,868
Then do you have a better idea?

314
00:27:22,120 --> 00:27:24,205
I'll find a way to make money with you.

315
00:27:24,289 --> 00:27:26,624
-Take every job I can--
-You're unidentified.

316
00:27:43,975 --> 00:27:45,977
-Isn't that Tae-ha?
-It's Tae-ha and Eun-sae.

317
00:27:47,479 --> 00:27:48,313
Tae…

318
00:27:49,105 --> 00:27:51,024
What's going on? Something seems off.

319
00:27:51,107 --> 00:27:52,942
Jang Tae-ha!

320
00:28:00,200 --> 00:28:02,744
-I think they had a fight.
-Is she crying?

321
00:28:05,747 --> 00:28:06,748
Ladies.

322
00:28:08,416 --> 00:28:09,626
What are you doing?

323
00:28:15,882 --> 00:28:17,050
Nothing at all.

324
00:28:19,761 --> 00:28:22,639
Something's going on with them, right?

325
00:28:22,722 --> 00:28:24,808
Something out of the ordinary, right?

326
00:28:24,891 --> 00:28:26,392
Talk.

327
00:28:26,476 --> 00:28:28,561
We've all got several decades
under our belts.

328
00:28:28,645 --> 00:28:31,481
You think we can't read a room? Tell us!

329
00:28:34,067 --> 00:28:37,362
We've been sensing something
for a few days now.

330
00:28:37,946 --> 00:28:41,533
Strangers have been
creeping into our quiet village.

331
00:28:42,242 --> 00:28:44,744
And on roads only ever used
by a few tractors,

332
00:28:44,828 --> 00:28:48,832
we saw a huge, black Mercedes-Benz.

333
00:28:48,915 --> 00:28:49,749
Tell us.

334
00:28:49,833 --> 00:28:51,626
What on earth is going on?

335
00:28:51,709 --> 00:28:54,295
-Tell us.
-Talk.

336
00:28:54,879 --> 00:28:58,258
-Talk!
-Tell us.

337
00:28:58,341 --> 00:28:59,759
Tell us.

338
00:29:01,511 --> 00:29:04,430
A prosecutor from Seoul?

339
00:29:07,600 --> 00:29:08,768
Then this whole thing

340
00:29:09,727 --> 00:29:13,231
was an act to save our Eun-sae,
who has no memory?

341
00:29:14,274 --> 00:29:18,319
I'm telling you this knowing
that Tae-ha will beat me to death.

342
00:29:18,987 --> 00:29:23,575
Because I think we could also use help
from you S.E.S ladies.

343
00:29:25,159 --> 00:29:27,161
-Okay.
-Goodness.

344
00:29:29,205 --> 00:29:31,791
HONG'S BOXING GYM

345
00:29:32,417 --> 00:29:34,544
Please help me, Mr. Hong.

346
00:29:34,627 --> 00:29:38,172
Jang Tae-ha listens to you.

347
00:29:38,256 --> 00:29:41,050
So please persuade him. Please?

348
00:29:41,134 --> 00:29:42,260
It's no use.

349
00:29:42,343 --> 00:29:45,638
Mr. Hong has already tried everything
to stop him.

350
00:29:45,722 --> 00:29:47,891
But you know he's as stubborn as a mule.

351
00:29:50,226 --> 00:29:51,477
That darned punk.

352
00:29:56,816 --> 00:29:57,942
What now?

353
00:29:59,402 --> 00:30:02,530
You despise gangsters, Eun-sae.

354
00:30:07,702 --> 00:30:09,412
I can't believe it.

355
00:30:12,874 --> 00:30:16,836
He promised me
that he would never use violence again.

356
00:30:17,670 --> 00:30:20,298
He's not one to break promises.

357
00:30:27,388 --> 00:30:29,515
How could Jang Tae-ha…

358
00:30:38,399 --> 00:30:39,651
Hey, so you're really…

359
00:30:39,734 --> 00:30:42,820
Can you prepare a two-month supply
of medicine for her?

360
00:30:43,738 --> 00:30:46,282
And something to calm her
when she's feeling down.

361
00:30:48,159 --> 00:30:51,204
Do you think doing this will change
how she feels about you?

362
00:30:52,997 --> 00:30:54,624
Go Eun-sae hates gangsters.

363
00:30:54,707 --> 00:30:57,126
Maybe hating me
will make it hurt a little less.

364
00:31:02,173 --> 00:31:03,508
That crazy bastard!

365
00:31:03,591 --> 00:31:07,971
This is why I was so against
Pil-seung boxing.

366
00:31:08,054 --> 00:31:12,475
If all you know is how to fight,
it's easy to go down that path.

367
00:31:14,143 --> 00:31:15,645
That's what I'm saying.

368
00:31:15,728 --> 00:31:19,023
I thought that punk
had gotten his act together.

369
00:31:19,107 --> 00:31:20,274
But back to being a thug?

370
00:31:21,234 --> 00:31:23,319
He's a lost cause, he is.

371
00:31:23,403 --> 00:31:24,737
Looking back now,

372
00:31:24,821 --> 00:31:27,365
it's a huge relief
you didn't walk down the aisle.

373
00:31:27,448 --> 00:31:28,366
Eun-sae.

374
00:31:29,325 --> 00:31:32,203
That jerk, Tae-ha. Just dump him already!

375
00:31:37,917 --> 00:31:39,836
I should get home.

376
00:31:59,522 --> 00:32:00,440
Tae-ha.

377
00:32:20,043 --> 00:32:21,669
There must be a way.

378
00:32:22,420 --> 00:32:24,922
Maybe there's nothing we can do right now,

379
00:32:25,923 --> 00:32:27,008
but one day,

380
00:32:28,051 --> 00:32:29,802
I'm sure there will be a way.

381
00:33:02,460 --> 00:33:05,171
I know saving lives is the priority,

382
00:33:06,214 --> 00:33:07,465
but you shouldn't get hurt.

383
00:33:12,929 --> 00:33:15,056
You can't underestimate the power of food.

384
00:33:15,556 --> 00:33:18,559
You need a full belly to do great things.

385
00:33:25,399 --> 00:33:27,735
All this while, every day,

386
00:33:28,319 --> 00:33:31,280
every moment must have felt like
walking a tightrope

387
00:33:32,323 --> 00:33:33,741
with that enormous burden.

388
00:33:38,454 --> 00:33:39,497
Thank you.

389
00:33:40,331 --> 00:33:43,167
As of now, we have no choice
but to send Eun-sae away

390
00:33:43,751 --> 00:33:45,545
if we want to save her, right?

391
00:33:48,840 --> 00:33:49,841
Yes.

392
00:33:56,097 --> 00:33:59,433
And is there anything we can do to help?

393
00:34:31,174 --> 00:34:32,008
Are you okay?

394
00:34:37,597 --> 00:34:38,931
I was so startled.

395
00:34:39,432 --> 00:34:41,475
Even so, how could you collapse like that?

396
00:34:42,059 --> 00:34:43,853
You need to learn to protect yourself.

397
00:34:46,814 --> 00:34:49,400
Easy for someone like you to say.

398
00:34:54,864 --> 00:34:55,907
Want me to teach you?

399
00:34:59,410 --> 00:35:02,288
First, get into this position.

400
00:35:02,371 --> 00:35:04,665
If someone attacks you head-on,

401
00:35:05,791 --> 00:35:08,002
you just need to turn your body like this.

402
00:35:09,837 --> 00:35:13,049
Just by turning away,
you can avoid a fatal injury.

403
00:35:13,841 --> 00:35:14,759
Let's try it.

404
00:35:16,344 --> 00:35:18,221
-That's it.
-Like this?

405
00:35:18,971 --> 00:35:21,057
And if someone attacks you from behind…

406
00:35:21,933 --> 00:35:23,684
Try grabbing me from behind.

407
00:35:26,270 --> 00:35:27,104
Like this?

408
00:35:27,939 --> 00:35:28,814
Then…

409
00:35:29,899 --> 00:35:30,983
Step on their foot,

410
00:35:31,484 --> 00:35:33,569
elbow them in the stomach,

411
00:35:33,653 --> 00:35:35,571
stick your leg out to trip them up…

412
00:35:38,199 --> 00:35:39,242
and run away.

413
00:35:46,082 --> 00:35:48,251
Okay, I'll give it a try.

414
00:35:50,044 --> 00:35:52,505
When someone attacks me from behind,

415
00:35:53,256 --> 00:35:54,632
I step on their foot,

416
00:35:55,132 --> 00:35:57,551
elbow them in the stomach,

417
00:35:57,635 --> 00:35:59,887
stick my leg out to make them fall,

418
00:36:00,388 --> 00:36:01,430
and run away.

419
00:36:02,431 --> 00:36:03,266
You're good.

420
00:36:04,809 --> 00:36:07,270
That's cool. It really works.

421
00:36:07,979 --> 00:36:09,480
Let me try one more time.

422
00:36:10,439 --> 00:36:11,274
Okay.

423
00:36:13,943 --> 00:36:14,777
And then…

424
00:36:24,412 --> 00:36:26,289
Step on their foot…

425
00:36:33,421 --> 00:36:36,757
It's a little hard to move if you do this.

426
00:37:00,072 --> 00:37:01,824
Jang Tae-ha.

427
00:37:06,704 --> 00:37:07,538
Go Eun-sae.

428
00:37:09,790 --> 00:37:11,792
Don't take it too hard.

429
00:37:14,378 --> 00:37:16,213
If you just keep living…

430
00:37:21,302 --> 00:37:22,803
everything passes.

431
00:37:28,768 --> 00:37:30,394
You just need to stay alive.

432
00:37:35,858 --> 00:37:37,777
What are you talking about?

433
00:37:44,283 --> 00:37:45,576
I'm sorry for startling you.

434
00:37:48,621 --> 00:37:50,373
For hurting you.

435
00:38:01,342 --> 00:38:02,510
The wind's cold.

436
00:38:03,886 --> 00:38:04,929
I'll get you a jacket.

437
00:38:43,676 --> 00:38:47,972
THE DAY OF THE ESCAPE

438
00:38:52,268 --> 00:38:54,478
-Looks delicious.
-Right, well…

439
00:38:54,562 --> 00:38:55,688
No particular reason.

440
00:38:55,771 --> 00:38:58,941
You just seemed so down because of Tae-ha,

441
00:38:59,817 --> 00:39:01,652
so, to cheer you up,

442
00:39:01,735 --> 00:39:05,823
I thought we'd all get together
and share a meal.

443
00:39:05,906 --> 00:39:07,074
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

444
00:39:08,075 --> 00:39:10,286
It's the tofu poke that you like.

445
00:39:10,369 --> 00:39:12,621
I made the tofu myself.

446
00:39:15,166 --> 00:39:16,000
Okay.

447
00:39:16,500 --> 00:39:18,377
Thank you so much.

448
00:39:19,378 --> 00:39:20,212
Everyone.

449
00:39:22,756 --> 00:39:23,924
Let's eat, okay?

450
00:39:24,008 --> 00:39:26,760
You know,

451
00:39:27,636 --> 00:39:30,681
I didn't see the tag
and accidentally bought a size small.

452
00:39:30,764 --> 00:39:31,807
Pity.

453
00:39:31,891 --> 00:39:34,101
Why don't you just wear it, Eun-sae?

454
00:39:35,728 --> 00:39:36,604
But this is…

455
00:39:37,813 --> 00:39:39,690
And this…

456
00:39:40,191 --> 00:39:42,568
I made this
when I still had my spiritual powers.

457
00:39:42,651 --> 00:39:44,737
Carry it with you. It'll be effective.

458
00:39:45,571 --> 00:39:47,114
-Okay.
-That's precious.

459
00:39:48,532 --> 00:39:49,575
Here!

460
00:39:49,658 --> 00:39:52,786
This is lion's mane liquor.

461
00:39:52,870 --> 00:39:53,746
Take it.

462
00:39:53,829 --> 00:39:55,498
But this is…

463
00:39:55,581 --> 00:39:57,750
Isn't this your most prized possession?

464
00:39:57,833 --> 00:40:01,504
You can find mushrooms everywhere
if you dig with a hoe.

465
00:40:01,587 --> 00:40:02,922
I can just make more.

466
00:40:03,005 --> 00:40:03,881
But…

467
00:40:09,053 --> 00:40:10,554
This much?

468
00:40:11,222 --> 00:40:13,057
Song-wol.

469
00:40:14,517 --> 00:40:16,185
What is all this, everyone?

470
00:40:16,685 --> 00:40:18,896
Are you all giving me gifts

471
00:40:20,481 --> 00:40:21,690
to cheer me up?

472
00:40:28,989 --> 00:40:30,032
TAFFY VILLAGE PHOTO CONTEST

473
00:40:30,115 --> 00:40:31,659
-This is us making taffy.
-Right?

474
00:40:31,742 --> 00:40:32,785
Yes, it is.

475
00:40:33,285 --> 00:40:35,788
-Look at this.
-Do you want a picture?

476
00:40:37,206 --> 00:40:38,082
At the karaoke bar.

477
00:40:39,124 --> 00:40:40,125
How pretty.

478
00:40:40,209 --> 00:40:42,962
That's a good one.
You look like an actress.

479
00:40:47,132 --> 00:40:48,217
This is you guys.

480
00:40:50,928 --> 00:40:52,429
What's wrong? We look great.

481
00:40:53,889 --> 00:40:56,058
You and Song-wol look great in this one.

482
00:40:56,559 --> 00:40:59,019
-How lovely.
-You look so pretty.

483
00:41:00,521 --> 00:41:04,483
I really love this village.

484
00:41:05,693 --> 00:41:08,070
The scenery is beautiful,

485
00:41:08,153 --> 00:41:10,489
and I love the sweet smell
of boiling taffy.

486
00:41:10,573 --> 00:41:11,699
Of course.

487
00:41:12,324 --> 00:41:13,158
Right?

488
00:41:13,659 --> 00:41:18,455
Being born and raised in Taffy Village,

489
00:41:18,539 --> 00:41:22,710
I learned that relationships
are like sweet taffy.

490
00:41:23,586 --> 00:41:27,881
Once you form a bond,
it's not easy to break it.

491
00:41:27,965 --> 00:41:28,966
That's right.

492
00:41:29,049 --> 00:41:32,720
And the warmer it gets,
the more it sticks.

493
00:41:32,803 --> 00:41:36,890
Even if you want to spit it out halfway,
it gets so stuck that you can't.

494
00:41:40,477 --> 00:41:41,604
That's why

495
00:41:42,146 --> 00:41:44,607
if it's meant to be, it'll stick.

496
00:41:45,107 --> 00:41:46,775
You're bound to meet again.

497
00:41:51,530 --> 00:41:52,531
When you think about it,

498
00:41:52,615 --> 00:41:55,200
saying that something is like taffy
is a good thing.

499
00:41:55,284 --> 00:41:57,745
I wonder how it came to be used
in a bad way.

500
00:41:59,580 --> 00:42:00,539
Tae-ha.

501
00:42:00,623 --> 00:42:02,249
You're here. Come.

502
00:42:02,333 --> 00:42:03,167
Hey.

503
00:42:05,878 --> 00:42:06,712
We have to go.

504
00:42:08,422 --> 00:42:09,256
Where?

505
00:42:11,925 --> 00:42:13,135
I'll tell you on the way.

506
00:42:15,804 --> 00:42:16,639
Go on.

507
00:42:17,890 --> 00:42:20,934
Everyone, choose your photos
and don't forget to save me some.

508
00:42:21,018 --> 00:42:22,603
-Sure.
-We'll be back.

509
00:42:22,686 --> 00:42:23,979
-All right.
-Okay.

510
00:42:24,063 --> 00:42:24,897
See you tomorrow.

511
00:42:56,303 --> 00:42:58,555
And we were just starting to get attached.

512
00:43:08,107 --> 00:43:09,358
Oh dear.

513
00:43:15,030 --> 00:43:16,240
We're going for fresh air?

514
00:43:17,616 --> 00:43:20,160
It's been tough lately.
You could use a change of scenery.

515
00:43:26,291 --> 00:43:27,376
You should get changed.

516
00:43:28,210 --> 00:43:30,754
We're going to see the ocean,
so dress warmly.

517
00:43:36,885 --> 00:43:41,348
DAEDANG PORT

518
00:43:48,856 --> 00:43:52,192
I think this is the first time
I've been this far from Taffy Village.

519
00:43:55,320 --> 00:43:58,073
We've seen the sea together before,
haven't we?

520
00:43:59,283 --> 00:44:00,117
Yes.

521
00:44:04,246 --> 00:44:05,748
Is something wrong?

522
00:44:06,665 --> 00:44:08,876
You haven't looked so good for a while.

523
00:44:09,626 --> 00:44:11,754
If you're tired, we can turn back.

524
00:44:13,088 --> 00:44:13,922
It's fine.

525
00:44:25,642 --> 00:44:28,020
What's wrong? What's going on?

526
00:44:52,503 --> 00:44:53,921
What's going on?

527
00:44:59,551 --> 00:45:00,552
Listen carefully.

528
00:45:01,053 --> 00:45:04,223
Don't come out no matter what,
and follow Gang-rok when he gets here.

529
00:45:04,723 --> 00:45:06,266
What? To where?

530
00:45:07,267 --> 00:45:08,560
Jang Tae-ha.

531
00:45:08,644 --> 00:45:09,645
Where are you…

532
00:45:16,944 --> 00:45:17,945
Get him!

533
00:45:24,326 --> 00:45:25,452
Jang Tae-ha!

534
00:45:34,169 --> 00:45:35,170
Open it!

535
00:45:41,677 --> 00:45:44,304
Get on, now! We don't have time!

536
00:45:54,314 --> 00:45:55,941
-Tae-ha.
-Go, now!

537
00:45:56,567 --> 00:45:58,735
We need to hurry!

538
00:46:00,737 --> 00:46:01,613
Now!

539
00:46:05,951 --> 00:46:08,245
He'll be right behind us.

540
00:46:09,997 --> 00:46:11,290
Hey, stop them!

541
00:46:40,694 --> 00:46:41,987
What's going on?

542
00:46:42,696 --> 00:46:43,906
Hurry up and explain.

543
00:46:45,198 --> 00:46:47,451
He's trying to save you.

544
00:46:47,534 --> 00:46:49,244
You're going to Japan now.

545
00:46:49,745 --> 00:46:51,413
What on earth are you talking about?

546
00:46:51,496 --> 00:46:52,915
Just go and stay there for now.

547
00:46:53,707 --> 00:46:55,918
That's the only way for you to live.

548
00:46:57,210 --> 00:46:58,337
What about Jang Tae-ha?

549
00:46:59,463 --> 00:47:00,797
Is he coming too?

550
00:47:02,007 --> 00:47:03,008
Yes.

551
00:47:16,980 --> 00:47:17,856
Eun-sae.

552
00:47:19,316 --> 00:47:21,485
Jang Tae-ha's really coming, right?

553
00:47:21,568 --> 00:47:22,444
Of course.

554
00:47:23,111 --> 00:47:26,198
If you just wait in there for a bit,
he'll be here in no time.

555
00:47:29,326 --> 00:47:30,327
Okay.

556
00:47:41,463 --> 00:47:42,381
Gang-rok.

557
00:47:42,464 --> 00:47:44,341
Jang Tae-ha…

558
00:48:16,957 --> 00:48:18,667
I'm Tae-ha's friend, Kaito.

559
00:48:18,750 --> 00:48:20,335
I'll escort you from here.

560
00:48:20,919 --> 00:48:23,255
-Please follow me.
-You can follow him.

561
00:48:23,839 --> 00:48:24,840
He's Tae-ha's man.

562
00:48:26,174 --> 00:48:28,885
I'll go to Tae-ha. Kaito.

563
00:48:34,558 --> 00:48:35,934
This way.

564
00:49:05,964 --> 00:49:07,424
We leave in ten minutes.

565
00:49:08,925 --> 00:49:09,760
Sorry?

566
00:49:11,011 --> 00:49:13,388
Then what about Jang Tae-ha?

567
00:49:36,369 --> 00:49:38,914
KAITO
BOARDING COMPLETE

568
00:50:05,190 --> 00:50:08,193
TIMER

569
00:51:17,053 --> 00:51:19,306
No. I don't want to go.

570
00:51:19,389 --> 00:51:21,558
Where would I go without Jang Tae-ha?

571
00:51:21,641 --> 00:51:24,394
Where is Jang Tae-ha? He was badly hurt.

572
00:51:27,063 --> 00:51:29,816
Jang Tae-ha is risking his life
to save you.

573
00:51:30,400 --> 00:51:31,443
Don't mess this up.

574
00:55:12,205 --> 00:55:13,832
How does blood taste after so long?

575
00:55:20,255 --> 00:55:22,382
Jang Tae-ha is Jang Tae-ha after all.

576
00:55:23,091 --> 00:55:24,884
You managed to save Prosecutor Go.

577
00:55:27,929 --> 00:55:31,141
But did you really think
that boat wouldn't have…

578
00:55:34,519 --> 00:55:35,520
my men on it?

579
00:55:49,576 --> 00:55:51,035
I was just playing with you.

580
00:55:52,203 --> 00:55:53,872
A bit of nostalgia.

581
00:55:54,372 --> 00:55:57,959
And I got to see you fight
like your life was on the line.

582
00:56:19,647 --> 00:56:21,983
Can you at least change the time
the boat leaves?

583
00:56:23,151 --> 00:56:24,360
I'm relying on you, Kaito.

584
00:56:24,444 --> 00:56:27,155
Just like in Namba, Osaka, ten years ago.

585
00:56:34,412 --> 00:56:35,747
Is someone listening in?

586
00:56:36,873 --> 00:56:40,376
I think so. I'm thinking of getting a boat
with a modified motor.

587
00:56:40,877 --> 00:56:41,753
That's too risky.

588
00:56:42,337 --> 00:56:44,923
If we go too fast,
the Coast Guard will spot us.

589
00:56:46,299 --> 00:56:47,467
We have to take the risk.

590
00:56:49,177 --> 00:56:50,595
I'll get the boat ready.

591
00:56:50,678 --> 00:56:52,680
And I can distract the Coast Guard.

592
00:56:52,764 --> 00:56:55,016
I looked into what you asked me to.

593
00:56:55,099 --> 00:56:56,351
It's possible.

594
00:56:58,228 --> 00:57:00,146
This boat leaves in three minutes.

595
00:57:00,230 --> 00:57:02,690
We don't have time.
We need to transfer quickly.

596
00:57:14,035 --> 00:57:15,537
TRANSFERRED TO MOTORBOAT
DEPARTING

597
00:57:38,810 --> 00:57:39,644
Chairman, sir.

598
00:57:40,603 --> 00:57:42,730
Prosecutor Go isn't on the cargo ship.

599
00:58:03,251 --> 00:58:05,253
What's happening…

600
00:58:12,552 --> 00:58:15,013
No! Jang Tae-ha!

601
00:58:16,014 --> 00:58:17,181
No!

602
00:58:20,727 --> 00:58:22,061
I'm Prosecutor Go Ji-won.

603
00:58:22,729 --> 00:58:24,022
We meet again, Prosecutor.

604
00:58:49,380 --> 00:58:51,049
OUR STICKY LOVE

605
00:59:37,679 --> 00:59:41,641
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi

